00:35:04,300 --> 00:35:06,667
- Come on, doctor,
you've a plane to catch.

761
00:35:06,667 --> 00:35:08,967
- One second, there's a
reward I must collect.

762
00:35:10,633 --> 00:35:12,500
- Just remember your
name is Neil Connery.

763
00:35:12,500 --> 00:35:13,900
Now get in the plane.

764
00:35:13,900 --> 00:35:15,500
- You have to leave
the account open.

765
00:35:15,500 --> 00:35:17,467
Max is waiting for
you at the airport.

766
00:35:17,467 --> 00:35:19,333
- [Tom] Double O
double entendre.

767
00:35:22,233 --> 00:35:24,433
- I hope I see you again.

768
00:35:24,433 --> 00:35:25,500
- I think she's neat.

769
00:35:29,400 --> 00:35:32,133
♪ Well shake it up baby, now ♪

770
00:35:32,133 --> 00:35:34,200
- [Joel] Man, it sounds
like the British invasion's

771
00:35:34,200 --> 00:35:35,600
waiting for a flight out.

772
00:35:37,100 --> 00:35:38,733
- [Tom] And when you
deplane in Malaga,

773
00:35:38,733 --> 00:35:41,033
you'll be greeted
by Manfred Mann.

774
00:35:46,733 --> 00:35:48,600
- They should be here.

775
00:35:48,600 --> 00:35:50,800
- Do I have enough time
to beat up the band?

776
00:35:53,067 --> 00:35:54,333
- [Joel] They call
it the mercy beat.

777
00:35:54,333 --> 00:35:56,333
In five minutes, you'll
be screaming for mercy.

778
00:35:56,333 --> 00:35:57,167
Thank you.

779
00:36:00,767 --> 00:36:02,667
- They're playing
a penguin song.

780
00:36:02,667 --> 00:36:04,900
(quacking)

781
00:36:06,633 --> 00:36:08,500
- [Tom] Hey, it's Moneypenny,
pull over, it's Moneypenny.

782
00:36:08,500 --> 00:36:09,467
- [Male] Thanks a lot.

783
00:36:09,467 --> 00:36:11,233
- [Joel] That's okay.

784
00:36:12,167 --> 00:36:13,733
- Will you marry me?

785
00:36:13,733 --> 00:36:16,367
- The telegram just came and
I left my dear little bride,

786
00:36:16,367 --> 00:36:18,900
Consuela, and all
of the other guests

787
00:36:18,900 --> 00:36:20,967
in front of the church.

788
00:36:20,967 --> 00:36:24,100
As you see, Max, I'm
getting married today.

789
00:36:24,100 --> 00:36:26,300
- [Tom] Caught Moneypenny.

790
00:36:26,300 --> 00:36:27,567
- Where is Yachuko?

791
00:36:29,033 --> 00:36:30,900
- Watch me dance.

792
00:36:30,900 --> 00:36:33,700
- [Joel] Oh, not
another bowl losing.

793
00:36:33,700 --> 00:36:36,267
- At first sight I
took you for an azalea.

794
00:36:36,267 --> 00:36:37,133
What have you lost now?

795
00:36:37,133 --> 00:36:38,367
- My necklace.

796
00:36:38,367 --> 00:36:40,700
Oh, it's so sweet to
see you again, doctor.

797
00:36:40,700 --> 00:36:42,367
- Same to you.

798
00:36:42,367 --> 00:36:44,433
- Hey, it's Bernie
from room 222.

799
00:36:44,433 --> 00:36:47,067
- Dr. Connery, you're
so very kind as usual.

800
00:36:47,067 --> 00:36:48,700
- [Neil] My pleasure,
I'm very kind by nature.

801
00:36:48,700 --> 00:36:50,200
- I'll remember that.

802
00:36:50,200 --> 00:36:51,433
- [Tom] Hair by Jim Henson.

803
00:36:51,433 --> 00:36:53,533
- [Neil] Why don't you
remember it tonight?

804
00:36:54,733 --> 00:36:56,367
- [Joel] Hey, who's
your favorite clown?

805
00:36:56,367 --> 00:36:57,200
- [Both] Bozo!

806
00:36:57,200 --> 00:36:58,700
- [Joel] Hey, that's me!

807
00:36:58,700 --> 00:36:59,800
- Come on, doctor.

808
00:36:59,800 --> 00:37:00,667
- Sorry.

809
00:37:02,500 --> 00:37:04,833
- My husband Fang, ha ha!

810
00:37:07,733 --> 00:37:10,033
- [Tom] This Friday on Streets.

811
00:37:10,033 --> 00:37:11,100
- [Joel] This must
be the traditional

812
00:37:11,100 --> 00:37:12,867
call to gambling in Monte Carlo.

813
00:37:16,400 --> 00:37:18,267
- Go out and get
some air, fatso.

814
00:37:18,267 --> 00:37:19,967
(shouting)

815
00:37:19,967 --> 00:37:21,233
- [Joel] It's a little
drafty in the winter

816
00:37:21,233 --> 00:37:22,900
but you can really stretch out.

817
00:37:26,933 --> 00:37:27,767
- Yachuko!

818
00:37:30,767 --> 00:37:32,367
- Hey, this isn't how
we left her with you!

819
00:37:32,367 --> 00:37:33,600
- [Tom] He who
withdraws the blade

820
00:37:33,600 --> 00:37:35,567
is right wise born
king of England.

821
00:37:37,500 --> 00:37:38,567
- Who's been here?

822
00:37:38,567 --> 00:37:40,533
- [Joel] Some guy with a knife.

823
00:37:40,533 --> 00:37:41,700
- Poor girl.

824
00:37:41,700 --> 00:37:43,900
She didn't have anything
to do with this.

825
00:37:43,900 --> 00:37:45,033
- But this is not Yachuko.

826
00:37:45,033 --> 00:37:47,000
- [Joel] There was no Yachuko.

827
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:48,333
- She's a double, I tell you.

828
00:37:48,333 --> 00:37:49,733
A good double but that's all.

829
00:37:49,733 --> 00:37:51,300
- Solid double down the line.

830
00:37:51,300 --> 00:37:52,967
- Are you sure?

831
00:37:52,967 --> 00:37:55,167
- Positive, I know
her pretty well.

832
00:37:55,167 --> 00:37:56,733
I've operated on her face.

833
00:37:57,867 --> 00:37:59,533
- That means that
they used her as bait

834
00:37:59,533 --> 00:38:00,800
to keep us off the track.

835
00:38:00,800 --> 00:38:02,300
- [Joel] Are you gonna
marry me or what?

836
00:38:02,300 --> 00:38:04,367
- If you wanna find the real
Yachuko and still alive,

837
00:38:04,367 --> 00:38:06,567
I've a feeling you'd
better get moving fast.

838
00:38:11,867 --> 00:38:12,700
- Ew.

839
00:38:16,367 --> 00:38:18,400
- Well, what have
you lost this time?

840
00:38:18,400 --> 00:38:19,400
- Oh, I've lost my lighter.

841
00:38:19,400 --> 00:38:20,933
- [Tom] And my dignity.

842
00:38:20,933 --> 00:38:22,467
- [Neil] Do you ever walk
upright like other people?

843
00:38:22,467 --> 00:38:25,500
- [Joel] Pantsuits from the
Mary Tyler Moore collection.

844
00:38:25,500 --> 00:38:27,900
- [Neil] If I were a
lighter, where would I go?

845
00:38:27,900 --> 00:38:29,533
- Oh there it is.

846
00:38:29,533 --> 00:38:30,367
- Excuse me.

847
00:38:31,567 --> 00:38:33,267
- [Neil] There it is
indeed, there you are.

848
00:38:33,267 --> 00:38:35,167
- [Tom] You have a
nip, er, cigarette?

849
00:38:37,667 --> 00:38:39,500
- Not in front of
Sir Walter Raleigh!

850
00:38:41,467 --> 00:38:42,567
- [Joel] Flint, Flint!

851
00:38:45,333 --> 00:38:46,600
- My reward.

852
00:38:46,600 --> 00:38:47,500
- [Tom] That's it?

853
00:38:49,100 --> 00:38:51,700
- You've got gorgeous
eyes, you know.

854
00:38:51,700 --> 00:38:53,767
- Oh, do you really like them?

855
00:38:53,767 --> 00:38:54,600
- Very much.

856
00:38:54,600 --> 00:38:55,700
- Can I have one?

857
00:38:58,767 --> 00:39:02,600
- [Joel] Oh Neil, this isn't
right, I don't think that--

858
00:39:02,600 --> 00:39:04,533
- Ew, she's got
(mumbling) on her face.

859
00:39:06,667 --> 00:39:08,867
- Secret Agent John Ivan Palmer.

860
00:39:08,867 --> 00:39:11,000
- And now you will
do whatever I want

861
00:39:12,367 --> 00:39:14,100
and you will tell me
everything I want to know.

862
00:39:14,100 --> 00:39:16,200
- [Joel] Let's talk hockey.

863
00:39:16,200 --> 00:39:18,367
- And you must obey me.

864
00:39:18,367 --> 00:39:19,800
Who sent you here?

865
00:39:19,800 --> 00:39:20,733
Thanatos?

866
00:39:20,733 --> 00:39:22,033
- Yes.

867
00:39:22,033 --> 00:39:22,867
- [Tom] Lip sync.

868
00:39:22,867 --> 00:39:24,667
- Who was their cheat?

869
00:39:24,667 --> 00:39:25,500
- Edward Clap?

870
00:39:26,633 --> 00:39:28,200
- Nobody knows.

871
00:39:28,200 --> 00:39:29,400
♪ The trouble I've seen ♪

872
00:39:29,400 --> 00:39:30,933
- What are they planning?

873
00:39:30,933 --> 00:39:32,567
- I don't know.

874
00:39:32,567 --> 00:39:35,433
- Do you know where
they've hidden Yachuko?

875
00:39:35,433 --> 00:39:36,900
- Yes.

876
00:39:36,900 --> 00:39:40,500
In (mumbling) villa near Malaga.

877
00:39:40,500 --> 00:39:42,700
Just past the
crossroad of Marbella.

878
00:39:42,700 --> 00:39:43,767
- By a Tom Thumb.

879
00:39:43,767 --> 00:39:45,167
- And is it heavily guarded?

880
00:39:46,733 --> 00:39:49,367
- It's surrounded by
a high tension fence

881
00:39:50,300 --> 00:39:51,767
and there's a machine gun too.

882
00:39:51,767 --> 00:39:53,267
- Whether that's
heavily guarded,

883
00:39:53,267 --> 00:39:56,167
I suppose it depends on your
definition of heavily guarded.

884
00:39:57,400 --> 00:39:58,767
- [Tom] Can I get your
brother's autograph?

885
00:39:58,767 --> 00:40:01,500
- You know, you've got
beautiful eyes too.

886
00:40:01,500 --> 00:40:03,433
- [Joel] No, you've
got beautiful eyes.

887
00:40:03,433 --> 00:40:05,600
- No, you've got beautiful eyes.

888
00:40:05,600 --> 00:40:07,800
- [Tom] And then of
course, oh my God.

889
00:40:07,800 --> 00:40:09,300
- Well, well, well.

890
00:40:09,300 --> 00:40:12,233
It looks like nobody in your
family is a rank amateur.

891
00:40:12,233 --> 00:40:14,533
- Let me get rearranged here.

892
00:40:14,533 --> 00:40:18,467
- To think this was supposed
to be my wedding night.

893
00:40:18,467 --> 00:40:21,967
- I'm sorry to break up
your little tete a tete

894
00:40:21,967 --> 00:40:24,300
but we've received
information that Yachuko

895
00:40:24,300 --> 00:40:27,200
is being held prisoner
outside Grenada.

896
00:40:27,200 --> 00:40:29,667
- That's funny, the
opposite direction.

897
00:40:29,667 --> 00:40:31,367
- Who told you that?

898
00:40:31,367 --> 00:40:32,300
- She told me.

899
00:40:32,300 --> 00:40:35,233
♪ She told me ♪

900
00:40:35,233 --> 00:40:37,733
No, let her go or we
might ruin everything.

901
00:40:40,533 --> 00:40:42,000
- [Tom] Wow, what a cigarette!

902
00:40:44,767 --> 00:40:45,800
- Maximum tanning.

903
00:40:48,333 --> 00:40:49,967
- [Joel] The
president's analyst.

904
00:40:51,067 --> 00:40:53,433
(whimpering)

905
00:40:54,567 --> 00:40:55,833
- You know, some people
just can't wake up

906
00:40:55,833 --> 00:40:57,267
no matter how many
alarms they set.

907
00:41:00,267 --> 00:41:01,500
- Stop now.

908
00:41:01,500 --> 00:41:02,933
- [Tom] Looks like you
got an extra game there.

909
00:41:04,467 --> 00:41:06,133
- [Joel] Sacre bleu.

910
00:41:07,667 --> 00:41:09,000
Sacre bleu, huh?

911
00:41:09,900 --> 00:41:11,700
- Oh yeah, sacre bleu.

912
00:41:11,700 --> 00:41:13,733
- [Joel] Let's go lift, man.

913
00:41:13,733 --> 00:41:15,733
- [Tom] Looking good.

914
00:41:15,733 --> 00:41:17,633
- It's alright, you can rest.

915
00:41:17,633 --> 00:41:18,900
Calm down.

916
00:41:18,900 --> 00:41:20,300
- [Tom] Mother Grimm
with her hair down.

917
00:41:20,300 --> 00:41:22,267
- They've made you
suffer, haven't they?

918
00:41:22,267 --> 00:41:25,000
How can they make such a
pretty girl suffer like that?

919
00:41:25,000 --> 00:41:26,667
- I'm asking myself
the same thing.

920
00:41:26,667 --> 00:41:28,733
- You mustn't be afraid of me.

921
00:41:28,733 --> 00:41:30,267
- [Joel] Here, have
some new Miller Clear.

922
00:41:30,267 --> 00:41:32,867
- [Female] We women understand
each other, don't we?

923
00:41:36,600 --> 00:41:37,833
Here.

924
00:41:37,833 --> 00:41:40,167
- [Tom] Water, it's
what's for dinner.

925
00:41:40,167 --> 00:41:41,400
- Drink.

926
00:41:41,400 --> 00:41:43,000
It'll do you good.

927
00:41:43,000 --> 00:41:44,533
- Bread will be out shortly.

928
00:41:44,533 --> 00:41:46,000
I'll let you look at the menu.

929
00:41:47,633 --> 00:41:49,167
- What do you want from me?

930
00:41:49,167 --> 00:41:50,800
I told you I don't
know anything.

931
00:41:50,800 --> 00:41:53,033
I really don't know anything.

932
00:41:53,033 --> 00:41:54,533
- [Female] Why are
you so obstinate?

933
00:41:54,533 --> 00:41:56,300
- [Joel] I get it
from my father.

934
00:41:56,300 --> 00:41:59,267
- We know that Ward
confided something to you.

935
00:41:59,267 --> 00:42:01,800
- It's not true,
no it's not true!

936
00:42:01,800 --> 00:42:03,267
It's not true!

937
00:42:03,267 --> 00:42:06,100
How many times do I have to
tell you I don't know anything?

938
00:42:06,100 --> 00:42:08,567
How can I convince you?

939
00:42:09,700 --> 00:42:12,100
- [Female] If you talk,
I shall reward you

940
00:42:12,100 --> 00:42:14,233
in a way you can't even imagine.

941
00:42:14,233 --> 00:42:15,233
- [Tom] I'll leave.

942
00:42:15,233 --> 00:42:16,200
- You'll live with me.

943
00:42:16,200 --> 00:42:17,033
- [Tom] Do you smoke?

944
00:42:17,033 --> 00:42:18,033
- Like a princess.

945
00:42:19,000 --> 00:42:20,600
- But I don't know anything.

946
00:42:20,600 --> 00:42:22,033
I swear it!

947
00:42:22,033 --> 00:42:22,967
(screaming)

948
00:42:22,967 --> 00:42:24,367
- [Joel] Welcome to noogie hell.

949
00:42:25,733 --> 00:42:27,000
- [Tom] Hello Vincent!

950
00:42:27,000 --> 00:42:28,033
- Hello Theo!

951
00:42:28,033 --> 00:42:29,033
- [Tom] Where is Vincent?

952
00:42:29,033 --> 00:42:31,100
- I am here, Theo.

953
00:42:31,100 --> 00:42:34,200
- [Tom] I feel like Gauguin
in freaking Tahiti here.

954
00:42:34,200 --> 00:42:36,300
- [Joel] Man, I'm
really hot, are you hot?

955
00:42:36,300 --> 00:42:37,533
Geez I'm hot.

956
00:42:41,867 --> 00:42:43,967
- (mumbling) you're my
knight in shining armor.

957
00:42:47,967 --> 00:42:50,767
- [Joel] Hey Greg, heard
it through the grapevine.

958
00:42:50,767 --> 00:42:52,433
(laughing)

959
00:42:52,433 --> 00:42:54,333
- [Female] Is that darn
thing going to work?

960
00:42:54,333 --> 00:42:56,433
- [Tom] Operation
double double O Hee-Haw.

961
00:42:56,433 --> 00:42:58,000
- [Neil] If my
calculations are correct,

962
00:42:58,000 --> 00:42:59,767
the short circuit
should cause a return

963
00:42:59,767 --> 00:43:01,967
of current capable of
blowing up the turret

964
00:43:01,967 --> 00:43:03,633
with the ammunition.

965
00:43:03,633 --> 00:43:05,833
- [Joel] Anyway, I got
Lulu backing me up.

966
00:43:09,200 --> 00:43:11,133
- Hooty hoo, hooty hoo!

967
00:43:17,333 --> 00:43:18,533
- This is your local
utility company

968
00:43:18,533 --> 00:43:21,067
reminding you to
call before you arc.

969
00:43:21,067 --> 00:43:23,400
(exploding)

970
00:43:24,267 --> 00:43:25,967
- [Joel] Fran Liebowitz!

971
00:43:27,833 --> 00:43:29,267
- [Tom] Follow zee everybody.

972
00:43:37,767 --> 00:43:40,333
(upbeat music)

973
00:43:43,700 --> 00:43:44,633
- Hi.

974
00:43:44,633 --> 00:43:46,100
Welcome to a segment we like

975
00:43:46,100 --> 00:43:48,733
to call the Sean and Neil
Show, Parallel Lives.

976
00:43:48,733 --> 00:43:51,467
- In which we look at
and contrast the careers

977
00:43:51,467 --> 00:43:54,267
of Sean Connery and his
brother Neil Connery.

978
00:43:54,267 --> 00:43:55,900
Let's start off
with today's movie.

979
00:43:55,900 --> 00:43:58,233
- Yeah, this line
represents Sean's life.

980
00:43:58,233 --> 00:44:00,500
This one represents Neil's life.

981
00:44:00,500 --> 00:44:01,800
I'll give you an example.

982
00:44:01,800 --> 00:44:03,933
Sean's acting
talent is discovered

983
00:44:03,933 --> 00:44:06,100
at an early age
and leads to a long

984
00:44:06,100 --> 00:44:07,733
and lucrative film career.

985
00:44:07,733 --> 00:44:09,667
- While Neil's talent
for selling light bulbs

986
00:44:09,667 --> 00:44:11,367
over the phone is
discovered leading

987
00:44:11,367 --> 00:44:13,000
to a long life of menial jobs

988
00:44:13,000 --> 00:44:14,633
and aimless drifting.

989
00:44:14,633 --> 00:44:17,100
- Well up here is when Sean

990
00:44:17,100 --> 00:44:19,000
gets his first million
dollar royalty check

991
00:44:19,000 --> 00:44:20,533
for the James Bond series.

992
00:44:20,533 --> 00:44:23,900
- While Neil gets his first
65 dollar unemployment check

993
00:44:23,900 --> 00:44:26,367
after being laid off
from the cheese factory.

994
00:44:26,367 --> 00:44:29,167
- Here Sean is declared
sexiest man alive

995
00:44:29,167 --> 00:44:30,467
by People Magazine.

996
00:44:30,467 --> 00:44:32,733
- While Neil is declared
the stinky cat man

997
00:44:32,733 --> 00:44:35,933
in room 4B by the other
tenants in his SRO hotel.

998
00:44:35,933 --> 00:44:38,400
- Here, Sean calls
the most powerful

999
00:44:38,400 --> 00:44:40,167
and influential
people in Hollywood

1000
00:44:40,167 --> 00:44:41,667
and is put through immediately.

1001
00:44:41,667 --> 00:44:43,833
- While Neil calls
Pizza Hut and is told

1002
00:44:43,833 --> 00:44:45,033
that they won't deliver to him

1003
00:44:45,033 --> 00:44:46,367
because of bounced checks.

1004
00:44:46,367 --> 00:44:49,667
- Here Sean is quoted as
saying during the making

1005
00:44:49,667 --> 00:44:52,333
of the Man Who Would Be King,
I had creative differences

1006
00:44:52,333 --> 00:44:53,900
with Director John Houston.

1007
00:44:53,900 --> 00:44:56,167
- While Neil is quoted
as saying my manager

1008
00:44:56,167 --> 00:44:58,100
at the Happy Chef won't
let me off for weekends.

1009
00:44:58,100 --> 00:44:59,600
What a dink, man.

1010
00:44:59,600 --> 00:45:03,067
- Here Sean goes to Spago's
and is seated immediately.

1011
00:45:03,067 --> 00:45:05,233
- While Neil's hot
plate malfunctioned

